# Build context exclusions. The context is the REPO ROOT for both images
# (api/Dockerfile and web-ui/Dockerfile), so this is the only .dockerignore that
# applies -- api/.dockerignore is inert and kept only to avoid implying otherwise.

# Dependencies and build output. The build output matters as much as .env does:
# without it a stale LOCAL build enters the context and can land beside the fresh
# one, which is the same class of defect as leaking a secret and considerably more
# likely to happen.
**/node_modules
**/dist
web-ui/dist
**/coverage

# A stale .tsbuildinfo from a composite build makes tsc skip .d.ts emission
# entirely -- the build "succeeds" and the image is missing its type output.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Both patterns are needed: .env.* does not match a bare .env.
.env
.env.*

# Not part of any build.
**/*.md
**/*.log
.git
.github
.githooks
.claude
docs
tests

# Uploaded card images live here locally and are a bind mount in production.
data
